    {
      "@id": "urn:uuid:c1381a0c-47be-4721-9022-ddec7d45b3fd",
      "@type": "mira:Evidence",
      "title": "dilations-nearer-neurons-than-constrictions",
      "description": {
        "@type": "Item",
        "format": "text/plain",
        "content": "Following ChR2 optogenetic activation at 458 nm, capillary dilations occur on average 16.1±14.3 µm from the nearest labeled pyramidal neuron while constrictions occur 21.9±14.6 µm away (4.3 mW/mm²; p<1e-4), and this spatial segregation is absent under control 552 nm illumination."
      },
      "sourceDocument": {
        "@id": "https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.95525",
