      "@type": "mira:Protocol",
      "title": "registration-doubles-vessel-count",
      "description": {
        "@type": "Item",
        "format": "text/plain",
        "content": "Rigid registration across time points and union of segmentation masks increases the number of identified vessel segments per FOV from 241±174 (single time point) to 412±281 (union across all time points; 507×507×250 µm, n=107 FOVs), while reducing mean squared error between acquisitions from 1306±747 to 0.008±0.003 signal units."
